adaptation-samsung-gts7xlwifi (0.0.6+git20260530164500.0000000.trixie) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Wi-Fi: make route-install reliable across boots (systemd service + shared helper).
    The NM dispatcher alone didn't reliably fire at boot. Add wlan-routes.service
    (oneshot, After=NetworkManager) running /usr/lib/adaptation-samsung-gts7xlwifi/
    wlan-routes-fix: a self-contained ~90s-retry helper that reads the address off the
    live Wi-Fi interface (the name varies swlan0/wlp1s0/wlanN across boots) and installs
    the network + default routes, which NM leaves unset (empty IP4.GATEWAY +
    noprefixroute). The 50-wlan-routes dispatcher now calls the same helper on
    up/dhcp4-change for mid-session reconnects. Service enabled via debian/links.
  * Firefox: force H.264 + cap fps for usable YouTube. Add usr/lib/firefox/defaults/
    pref/zz-halium-video-gts7xlwifi.js: disable AV1/VP9/WebM (no GPU/VAAPI video decode
    on this Halium device, so VP9/AV1 software-decode lagged; H.264 is ~4-6x cheaper)
    and set layout.frame_rate=60 to ease fullscreen compositing on the 120Hz panel.

 -- Mustafa Kahraman <mkahraman341@gmail.com>  Sat, 30 May 2026 16:45:00 +0000

adaptation-samsung-gts7xlwifi (0.0.5+git20260530075616.0000000.trixie) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Wi-Fi: add NetworkManager dispatcher script to install routes on connect.
    On this device NM gets the DHCP lease (IP + DNS + 'routers' option) but fails
    to install the connected route or the default route (IP4.GATEWAY ends up
    empty) -> "connected but no internet". etc/NetworkManager/dispatcher.d/
    50-wlan-routes reinstalls them from the NM-exported env on each wlp1s0 up /
    dhcp4-change. Non-disruptive (does not toggle the interface — toggling WLAN
    via nmcli down/up wedges the cnss driver on this device).

 -- Mustafa Kahraman <mkahraman341@gmail.com>  Sat, 30 May 2026 07:56:16 +0000

adaptation-samsung-gts7xlwifi (0.0.4+git20260529234841.0000000.trixie) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Auto-rotate: enable working automatic screen rotation (display + touch).
    - debian/postinst: set sensorfw accelerometer transformation_matrix to
      "0,-1,0,1,0,0,0,0,1" in /etc/sensorfw/sensord-hybris.conf so the reported
      orientation matches the physical device in all four orientations (the raw
      hybris accel axes were swapped + one inverted relative to the panel).
    - Enable sensorfwd.service (provides the accelerometer data; iio-sensor-proxy
      is D-Bus-activated on top of it).
    - Stop masking iio-sensor-proxy.service (revert the A3 landscape-lock from
      0.0.3) so phosh receives orientation events and rotates.
    The landscape touch calibration matrix (98-touch-calib.rules) is kept: it is
    the base digitizer<->panel alignment, and the compositor rotates touch on top
    of it, so touch follows the display correctly in every orientation.
  * Verified on-device: display + touch both rotate correctly in all orientations.

 -- Mustafa Kahraman <mkahraman341@gmail.com>  Fri, 29 May 2026 23:48:41 +0000

adaptation-samsung-gts7xlwifi (0.0.3+git20260529225627.0000000.trixie) trixie; urgency=medium

  * Display/input/power fixes (fold in manual bring-up tweaks):
    - etc/udev/rules.d/98-touch-calib.rules: set LIBINPUT_CALIBRATION_MATRIX
      "0 1 0 -1 0 1" on sec_touchscreen so touch matches the locked-landscape
      phosh output.
    - Mask iio-sensor-proxy.service: keep the display in landscape so the fixed
      touch matrix above stays correct (no auto-rotate flipping it).
    - Mask suspend.target / sleep.target / hibernate.target / hybrid-sleep.target
      / suspend-then-hibernate.target: idle-suspend cannot resume on this device
      and leaves it black/frozen, so block sleep entirely until resume works.

